M1 is the interesting one: it is not a made-up weakening but the code that was in the
repository this morning, and two fixtures name it.

== 7. Wiring

No wiring change was needed, which is why this went red only in CI and only after the guard
had already been run on both roots many times. Both roots invoke the pair, and the gate
count and labels are unchanged:

    .github/workflows/ci.yml          python3 scripts/ci/test-check-evidence-commands.py
                                      python3 scripts/ci/check-evidence-commands.py
    scripts/verify-in-docker.sh       "documented commands can be run: python3 scripts/ci/test-check-evidence-commands.py && python3 scripts/ci/check-evidence-commands.py"

The container is a third checkout, and it reproduces the CI verdict when its tree is clean.
The entry point mounts the tree it was launched from, so the runs below differ only in that
tree and in which version of the gate the tree carried. Image `chaos-verify:frozen`, one
label:

$ IMAGE_TAG=chaos-verify:frozen bash scripts/verify-in-docker.sh --only 'documented commands'

    tree=depth-1 clone of 778d4da, node_modules absent, gate before the change
